    "lawCode": "Add §630-g, Tax L; add §97-yyyy, St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3570\n\nSPONSOR: SERRANO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the tax law and the state finance law,\nin relation to gifts for the support of the New York state council on\nthe arts\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to provide the New York State Council on the\nArts with additional resources.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThe bill would allow taxpayers to make a gift to the New York State\nCouncil on the Arts through a \"check-off\" on their New York State\npersonal income tax return. Gifts would have to be made in whole dollar\namounts and would not reduce the amount of tax owed by the donor. All\ngifts made by taxpayers would be deposited to a special arts fund in the\njoint custody of the State Comptroller and the Commissioner of Taxation\nand Finance. Amounts in the arts fund would be appropriated by the\nLegislature and paid out to the New York State Council on the Arts.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill would increase funding for the New York State Council on the\nArts without impacting current State funds. Due to severe budgetary\nconstraints, New York State Council on the Arts support has been signif-\nicantly lagging ever since the housing crises and recession.  This\ndeclining support has had a devastating effect upon many of New York's\ncultural institutions as well as related or dependent businesses and\nemployees. This bill would give New York taxpayers the opportunity to\nuse the New York State personal income tax form as a mechanism for\nmaking voluntary contributions to foster arts and cultural programming\nthroughout the state.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2015-2016: S948-A-REFERRED TO INVESTIGATIONS AND GOVERNMENT OPERATIONS\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone. Authorizes voluntary donations.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act would take effect immediately.\n",
