  "chapter": 467,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 14 Chapter 467\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 3570, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the tax law and the state finance law, in relation\n        to gifts for the support of the New York state  council  on  the\n        arts\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  I  strongly  believe  that  New  York  State taxpayers should have the\nopportunity to support the New York State Council on  the  Arts  (NYSCA)\nthrough  a  voluntary gift contributed through their personal income tax\nreturn. This bill accomplishes that end and provides additional  support\nto  NYSCA  through  a  \"check-off\" on New York State personal income tax\nreturns.\n \n  All gifts made by taxpayers would then be deposited to a special  arts\nfund  in the joint custody of the State Comptroller and the Commissioner\nof Taxation and Finance, appropriated by the Legislature, and then  paid\nout directly to NYSCA.\n \n  Because the agreed upon chapter amendment clarifies that the intention\nof  the  bill  is  to provide additional resources to the New York State\nCouncil for the Arts, I am signing this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2019
 },
